id: pm-ts-starter-48t1
title: Drop inert pm manifest key and guard the closed manifest vocabulary
description: "pm-cli's extension-manifest vocabulary is a closed set of 18 keys; since pm-cli 2026.8.19 any other manifest.json key yields a manifest_unknown_key warning. This repo's manifest carried an inert top-level \"pm\": {\"compatibility\": \"v2\"} key that nothing in src/, scripts/, or test/ reads. It made downstream strict assertions (unbraind/pm-linear PRs #75/#76 expect finding codes exactly ['pm_min_version_unmet']) fail with an extra manifest_unknown_key code. This change deletes only that key, bumps the @unbrained/pm-cli devDependency pin from 2026.8.15 to 2026.8.22 (the older CLI cannot detect unknown keys), adds test/manifest-vocabulary.test.ts asserting zero unknown-key findings via checkExtensionManifestCompatibility against the exact pinned version, and updates smoke.test.ts to use 'list --all' instead of the deprecated 'list-all' alias whose stderr deprecation warning masked the read-buffer overrun runPm must surface."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-22T17:57:54.807Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-22T17:58:36.342Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-22T17:58:36.317Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-22T17:58:36.317Z"
claim_principal: ox-alpha
author: ox-alpha
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-22T17:58:08.440Z",ox-alpha,"Regression test verified: with 'pm' key re-added, test/manifest-vocabulary.test.ts fails with code manifest_unknown_key (path pm); after removal it passes. npm test: 149 tests, 149 pass, 0 fail. release:check exit 0 (no changelog script fix needed; unbounded-read flags already present). ./node_modules/.bin/pm health --strict-exit exit 0. Pre-existing smoke.test.ts failure (global pm 2026.8.21 deprecation warning for list-all masking the ENOBUFS overrun message) fixed by switching to non-deprecated 'list --all'; assertion strength unchanged."
files[5]{path,scope}:
